<title>UK: Novorossiisk still closed due to heavy swell.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk still closed due to heavy swell.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Black Sea oil port of Novorossiisk remained shut on Friday due to a heavy swell, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The port was closed at 0850 pm (local time) on Wednesday by a force seven gale.</p>
<p>The port was also closed for 33 hours last weekend.</p>
<p>Loadings are now running around two days behind schedule, the shipping source said.</p>
<p>Three crude tankers waited at anchor. One was scheduled to load at berth number one, which can accommodate vessels of up to 130,000 tonnes. The others were due to load at berth two.</p>
<p>The other Black Sea oil terminals and the Baltic port of Ventspils were all reported open.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5387</p>
</text>
